.Dd August 4, 2026
.Dt COLD 9
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cold
.Nd indicate that the system is still booting
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/systm.h
.Vt extern int cold;
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The global variable
.Va cold
is non-zero while the kernel is still performing early boot
and device configuration.
It is initialized to
.Dv 1
during machine-dependent startup and is set to
.Dv 0
when autoconfiguration has finished.
.Pp
Kernel code uses
.Va cold
to decide whether the system is still in the early boot phase,
when sleeping or relying on fully configured devices may not be
appropriate.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr config_intrhook 9 ,
.Xr kern_reboot 9
